{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThis epic was authored with a scope that was already partly false when it was written. Its original first comment asserted every claim was verified on `083620b0`; a full re-census on `50d5a36539d` found that the commits invalidating three of its five planned slices were all ancestors of `083620b0` itself. The second comment on this ticket records that census in full, per premise, with the invalidating commit and its date. The epic has been narrowed to what is actually live. Every figure below is measured on `50d5a36539d`.\n\n**Dropped as satisfied-on-arrival, not as work deferred.** The original criterion 4 (one precedence composer, one file discovery, `config.py` under the cap) is already true: `_resolve` (`config.py:353`) and `resolve_with_sources` (`:609`) both delegate to the single composer `_ordered_layers` (`:251`), `_discover_project_config` has one definition (`_config_sources.py:166`), and `config.py` is 630 lines against a cap of 800. `_ordered_layers` landed in `f23a976ea00` on 2026-06-16. The original criterion 5's registry half is likewise already true: `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` derives names by AST scan and ships fail-closed guards for unregistered and stale helper rows, and `docs/env-vars.md` holds 110 generated rows. Its `KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` hand-lists 9 helper *functions*, not canonical names. The original criterion 5's `REBAR_HLC=0` CHANGELOG item is dropped because that spelling has zero references in `src docs scripts` — it has no subject.\n\n**What remains.** ADR 0111 forbids internal shims, and two survive: `_engine_support/resolver.py`, a pure re-export of 9 names from `rebar._ids` with 51 importers, and 7 back-compat re-exports in `reducer/_processors.py` with 9 importing modules. ADR 0116 retired the config and env alias tables but left dead scaffolding behind — `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` is an explicitly empty dict (`_config_sources.py:299`), `_map_legacy_env` is a no-op returning its input (`:302`), and 6 sites still consume them. `_deprecations.py` carries 13 warn-class tombstones beside 6 error rows, all with a real `removed_in` of `v1.0.0` (AST-counted over the `_tomb` calls). Unknown `[llm]` keys are still silently ignored even under `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error`, because `[llm]` is a reserved section (`_config_sections.py:211`, skipped at `:225`). Two test hooks are still read by production code, each already marked `# read-via:`: `REBAR_HLC_NOW` (`_store/hlc.py:42`) and `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` (`_commands/compact_txn.py:187`). The `github-api` canary heartbeat source survives at `scripts/canary_bridge.py:141,143,687`.\n\nThe operator ruled (2026-09-06): hard cutover, no aliases, warn tombstones removed, error rows kept with real `removed_in` versions, unknown-key warnings kept as the forward-compatibility mechanism and extended to `[llm]`. That ruling stands and is unaffected by the narrowing.\n\nOperator sanction recorded here: the tombstone-prune and test-hook stories remove censused `env_var` mechanisms, so each runs `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` in the same change (`tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364`; precedent commit 81da792) and says so in its commit message.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No importer of `rebar._engine_support.resolver` or of the `reducer/_processors.py` re-exports remains, and both shims are deleted. Checked by an AST importer census and `make verify` in each shim story.\n- [ ] No dead alias scaffolding remains: `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`, `_map_legacy_env`, and all 6 consumer sites are gone. Checked by a repo-wide grep for both names in the scaffolding story.\n- [ ] `_deprecations.py` holds exactly the 6 error rows, each with a real `removed_in`; no warn-class row remains. Checked by an AST count over `_tomb` calls in the tombstone story.\n- [ ] An unknown key under `[llm]` warns under the same policy as any other section, and hard-errors under `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error`. Checked by the `[llm]` story's tests against both policy settings.\n- [ ] `REBAR_HLC_NOW` and `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` are not read by production code; tests inject the clock and the rename barrier through a test-owned child-process hook. Checked by each hook story's grep of `src/` and its child-process tests.\n- [ ] The `github-api` canary heartbeat source is retired and `status` is the only accepted value. Checked by the canary story's tests.\n\n## Child decomposition\nEight thin slices. The two shim stories are already filed and land first; nothing else depends on them, so the rest may proceed in parallel once they land.\n\n- S1a `insanitary-divine-moa` — migrate 51 resolver-shim importers to `rebar._ids`, delete the shim: criterion 1. FILED.\n- S1b `censurable-exotic-snake` — repoint the 7 `reducer/_processors.py` re-exports across 9 modules, delete them: criterion 1. FILED.\n- S2a — delete the dead `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` / `_map_legacy_env` scaffolding and its 6 consumers: criterion 2.\n- S2b — prune the 13 warn-class tombstones, keep the 6 error rows: criterion 3.\n- S2c — warn on unknown `[llm]` keys under the standard unknown-key policy: criterion 4.\n- S3a — move `REBAR_HLC_NOW` out of production into a test-owned child-process hook: criterion 5. Sized separately from S3b because it has 25 call sites across 4 test modules, 18 of them passing the var to child processes via `env_extra`, so `monkeypatch` cannot replace it.\n- S3b — move `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` out of production into the same hook: criterion 5. One production read and one test call site.\n- S4 — retire the `github-api` canary heartbeat source: criterion 6."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793378861934033608,"uuid":"89edaabf-8685-4a40-9583-f1dcad3dbd0c"}